From b663ce86bdacba7bbb5b843fecde906195790596 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:54:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] virtio/fs: serve no extended attributes on a read-only share

A read-only share's passthrough runs with xattr support off: its first
getxattr or listxattr answers ENOSYS, which the guest's FUSE keeps, and
every later one fails EOPNOTSUPP in the guest. Wine asks two extended
attributes of every directory entry it lists, under one process-wide
lock; over a share each was a round trip to the host (37 us on an idle
VM, far more on a busy one), and a game that lists its 10,000 resource
files at startup sat on a black window for minutes.

Assisted-by: Claude Code: claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
---
 src/devices/src/virtio/fs/device.rs | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/devices/src/virtio/fs/device.rs b/src/devices/src/virtio/fs/device.rs
index 27aacee2..a1b11cbd 100644
--- a/src/devices/src/virtio/fs/device.rs
+++ b/src/devices/src/virtio/fs/device.rs
@@ -88,6 +88,9 @@ impl Fs {
             root_dir,
             semantics,
             attr_timeout,
+            // A read-only share serves no extended attributes: the first getxattr or listxattr answers ENOSYS, which
+            // the guest's FUSE keeps, so later ones fail EOPNOTSUPP without a round trip to the host.
+            xattr: !read_only,
             ..Default::default()
         });
 
